      "deferred_scope": "Captured territory now uses persistent weighted local demographic/tax baselines plus a conserved local-population allocation ledger nested in the canonical state population owner. Native state, occupier, and rebels compete for the same local residents; service, deaths, displacement, taxation scale, revolt manpower, and governed recruitment update that ledger. Material revolts have autonomous recruitment, route interdiction, and counterinsurgency contact/battle through conserved formation losses. Dynamic polities have sovereign commands, institutions, monthly taxation/recruitment, interstate participation, and physical regional market/economy access. Full household-level settlement economy, local justice, epidemic propagation, and independent per-settlement production owners remain deferred."
